More Vulnerabilities That Can Be Paid (581–590)
581. Improper Validation of API Notification Subscriptions
Notification Subscription Manipulation
Attackers modify notification subscriptions to receive alerts meant for other users.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
582. Insecure Handling of OAuth Client Secrets
OAuth Client Secret Exposure
Client secrets are exposed in mobile apps or frontend code.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $10,000
583. Improper Validation of Bulk Import APIs
Bulk Import Data Manipulation
Bulk import endpoints accept manipulated datasets affecting backend systems.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $7,000
584. Insecure Handling of Email Template Systems
Email Template Injection
Attackers inject malicious content into email templates sent to users.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
585. Improper Validation of File Sharing Tokens
File Sharing Token Guessing
File-sharing tokens can be predicted or reused to access private documents.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $7,000
586. Insecure Handling of Application Deployment Scripts
Deployment Script Exposure
Deployment scripts reveal internal infrastructure details or credentials.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $9,000
587. Improper Authorization in Billing APIs
Billing API Authorization Bypass
Attackers manipulate billing APIs to view or modify financial information.
💰 Typical payout: $700 – $12,000
588. Insecure Handling of Push Notification Tokens
Push Token Exposure
Push notification tokens exposed allow attackers to send unauthorized messages.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
589. Improper Validation of Data Export Filters
Export Filter Authorization Bypass
Attackers manipulate export filters to download unauthorized data.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $7,000
590. Insecure Handling of System Monitoring Dashboards
Monitoring Dashboard Exposure
Monitoring dashboards reveal system metrics, internal endpoints, or infrastructure details.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $8,000
✅ Reality of bug bounty programs
Even though there are hundreds of vulnerability types, most large rewards come from a few major categories:
SQL Injection
Cross-Site Scripting
Server-Side Request Forgery
Remote Code Execution
Broken Access Control
Bug hunters often discover them using tools like:
Burp Suite
Nmap
FFUF
OWASP ZAP
